"Use timer (https://help.audible.com/s/article/use-timer)\nciteturn764view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/use-timer\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 127\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Android App settings Ask A Question iOS Listening+2\nL13: ## Use timer\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 3, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Use timer\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: use-timer\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: The Audible timer allows you to control when your audiobook will stop playing so you never lose your place again.\nL29: \nL30: Note: The timer feature is available only in the Audible app.\nL31: \nL32: In this article:\nL33:   * 【1†How to set the timer?】\nL34:   * 【2†How to extend your timer while it's running?】\nL35:   * 【3†How to extend your timer when it ends?】\nL36:   * 【4†How to turn on or off your shake-to-extend setting?】\nL37:   * 【5†How to use the timer with iOS Live Activity?】\nL38: ## How to set the timer?\nL39: \nL40:   1. Open your player while a title is playing.\nL41:   2. Select the Timer icon.\nL42:   3. Choose a preset time or create and save a custom length.\nL43:   4. Once time is up, your audiobook will stop playing.\nL44: ## How to extend your timer while it's running?\nL45: \nL46: If you'd like to change the timer while it's still counting down, you can overwrite it with a new time.\nL47: \nL48:   1. Open your player while a title is playing.\nL49:   2. Select the Timer icon at the bottom of the player or the “countdown banner” on top of the cover of the book\nL50:   3. Select a new time from the menu to overwrite the current timer.\nL51: ## How to extend your timer when it ends?\nL52: \nL53: When the timer ends, you'll get an alert. You can choose to extend the timer for the same amount of time or reset it with a new time.\nL54: \nL55: To extend your timer for the same amount of time, you can shake your phone within 30 seconds of the audio starting to fade.\nL56: ## How to turn on or off your shake-to-extend setting?\nL57: \nL58: You can change your timer settings anytime in the app.\nL59: \nL60:   1. Go to your Profile.\nL61:   2. Select the Settings gear icon.\nL62:   3. Select Player.\nL63:   4. Swipe to Timer.\nL64:   5. Toggle Shake to extend on or off.\nL65: ## How to use the timer with iOS Live Activity?\nL66: \nL67: iOS Live Activity is automatically turned on for all iPhones with iOS 17.0 or later. Whenever you set your timer, the Timer Live Activity will be visible from your phone's lock screen or dynamic island so you can see the time remaining without opening your iOS device.\nL68:   * For all iOS devices, you can shake your phone to extend the timer.\nL69:   * For all iOS devices with iOS 17.0 or later, you can select Live Activity from the lock screen to access your timer.\nL70:   * On all iPhone 14 Pros, you can select Live Activity on Apple's Dynamic Island to access your timer.\nL71: \nL72: Note: You can allow Audible Live Activities for Audible in your device settings. You can also accept or reject Live Activities from the Audible app when you see the Timer Live Activity for the first time.\nL73: Did this answer your question?\nL74: \nL75: 【6†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL76: \nL77: \nL78: \nL79: 【7†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL80: \nL81:  Back to top\nL82: \nL83: 【8†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL84: \nL85: 【9†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL86: ## Need more assistance?\nL87: \nL88: 【10†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL89: \nL90: \nL91: \nL92: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL93: \nL94: \nL95: \nL96: Worst\nL97: \nL98: 1\nL99: \nL100: 2\nL101: \nL102: 3\nL103: \nL104: 4\nL105: \nL106: 5\nL107: \nL108: 6\nL109: \nL110: 7\nL111: \nL112: Best\nL113: \nL114: \nL115: \nL116: Region\nL117: \nL118: United States\nL119: \nL120: Language\nL121: \nL122: English\nL123: \nL124: Loading\nL125: \nL126: Use timer 【11†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSet narration speed (https://help.audible.com/s/article/set-narration-speed?language=en_US)\nciteturn764view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/set-narration-speed?language=en_US\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 119\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Android Ask A Question Cloud Player iOS Listening+3\nL13: ## Set narration speed\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 3, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Set narration speed\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: set-narration-speed\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: You can access the narration speed setting right from your player. The default setting is 1.0x, but you can customize your speed based on whether you want to hear the narration slower or faster and set a different narration speed for each title in your library.\nL29: \nL30: In this article:\nL31:   * 【1†How can I change the narration speed for a particular title?】\nL32:   * 【2†How can I change the default narration speed?】\nL33:   * 【3†How can I change the narration speed in the Cloud Player?】\nL34: ## How can I change the narration speed for a particular title?\nL35: \nL36: You can set an individual narration speed in the app for each title in your library. That speed will be saved for that title across apps.\nL37: \nL38: In the app\nL39: \nL40:   1. Select a title to play.\nL41:   2. Open your player.\nL42:   3. Select the Speed icon at the bottom of the screen.\nL43:   4. Choose your desired setting.\nL44: ## How can I change the default narration speed?\nL45: \nL46: Changing the narration speed in your app Player settings will make this your default speed for all new listens.\nL47: \nL48: In the app Player settings\nL49: \nL50:   1. Select Profile.\nL51:   2. Select the Settings gear icon.\nL52:   3. Select Player.\nL53:   4. Select Narration Speed.\nL54:   5. Select Default.\nL55:   6. Choose your desired setting.\nL56: \nL57: Note: You can set a different default speed per device, for example a default speed of 1.75x on your phone but 1.25x on your tablet.\nL58: ## How can I change the narration speed in the Cloud Player?\nL59: \nL60:   1. Select a title to play.\nL61:   2. Select Play.\nL62:   3. Select the Speed icon at the bottom of the Player.\nL63:   4. Choose your desired setting.\nL64: \nL65: Did this answer your question?\nL66: \nL67: 【4†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL68: \nL69: \nL70: \nL71: 【5†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL72: \nL73:  Back to top\nL74: \nL75: 【6†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL76: \nL77: 【7†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL78: ## Need more assistance?\nL79: \nL80: 【8†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL81: \nL82: \nL83: \nL84: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL85: \nL86: \nL87: \nL88: Worst\nL89: \nL90: 1\nL91: \nL92: 2\nL93: \nL94: 3\nL95: \nL96: 4\nL97: \nL98: 5\nL99: \nL100: 6\nL101: \nL102: 7\nL103: \nL104: Best\nL105: \nL106: \nL107: \nL108: Region\nL109: \nL110: United States\nL111: \nL112: Language\nL113: \nL114: English\nL115: \nL116: Loading\nL117: \nL118: Set narration speed 【9†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nManage your auto-play settings (https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-your-auto-play-settings?language=en_US)\nciteturn764view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-your-auto-play-settings?language=en_US\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 143\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: App settings Ask A Question Listening Player Player tools\nL13: ## Manage your auto-play settings\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 3, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Manage your auto-play settings\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: manage-your-auto-play-settings\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: Control how titles play automatically in the Audible app. You can have your next selected title play automatically or discover related titles through previews when your current listen ends. For additional player options, please visit 【1†View player settings】.\nL29: \nL30: In this article:\nL31:   * 【2†How do I turn on Up next titles?】\nL32:   * 【3†How do I add titles to my Up next list?】\nL33:   * 【4†How do I edit titles in my Up next list?】\nL34:   * 【5†How do I turn on related title previews?】\nL35: ## How do I turn on Up next titles?\nL36: \nL37: You can have your selected titles play automatically without interruption.\nL38: \nL39:   1. Go to your Profile.\nL40:   2. Select the Settings gear icon.\nL41:   3. Select Player.\nL42:   4. Scroll to Continuous listening.\nL43:   5. Toggle Up next titles on.\nL44: ## How do I add titles to my Up next list?\nL45: \nL46: You can add titles to your Up next list directly from your Library. This feature is only available in the app.\nL47: \nL48: Using the 3-dot More menu:\nL49: \nL50:   1. Go to your Library.\nL51:   2. Select your title's 3-dot More menu.\nL52:   3. Select Play next.\nL53: \nL54: Using select and hold:\nL55: \nL56:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL57:   2. Go to your Library.\nL58:   3. Find the title you want to play next.\nL59:   4. Select and hold on the title.\nL60:   5. Select Play Next.\nL61: ## How do I edit titles in my Up next list?\nL62: \nL63:   1. Go to the player screen of your current listen.\nL64:   2. Select the Chapters menu.\nL65:   3. Select Up next.\nL66:   4. Select the 3-dot More menu next to the title you want to edit.\nL67:   5. Choose from the following options:\nL68:      * Title details\nL69:      * Share\nL70:      * Move to top\nL71:      * Move up\nL72:      * Move down\nL73:      * Move to bottom\nL74:      * Remove from queue\nL75: ## How do I turn on related title previews?\nL76: \nL77: Discover new titles through automatic previews when your current listen ends.\nL78: \nL79:   1. Go to your Profile.\nL80:   2. Select the Settings gear icon.\nL81:   3. Select Player.\nL82:   4. Scroll to Continuous listening.\nL83:   5. Toggle Recommended titles on.\nL84: \nL85: Note:\nL86: \nL87:   * Related title previews will only play if you don't have another title queued up to play next.\nL88:   * You can toggle Recommended titles off if you wish to stop the auto-play of related titles.\nL89: \nL90: Did this answer your question?\nL91: 【6†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL92: \nL93: \nL94: \nL95: 【7†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL96: \nL97:  Back to top\nL98: \nL99: 【8†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL100: \nL101: 【9†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL102: ## Need more assistance?\nL103: \nL104: 【10†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL105: \nL106: \nL107: \nL108: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL109: \nL110: \nL111: \nL112: Worst\nL113: \nL114: 1\nL115: \nL116: 2\nL117: \nL118: 3\nL119: \nL120: 4\nL121: \nL122: 5\nL123: \nL124: 6\nL125: \nL126: 7\nL127: \nL128: Best\nL129: \nL130: \nL131: \nL132: Region\nL133: \nL134: United States\nL135: \nL136: Language\nL137: \nL138: English\nL139: \nL140: Loading\nL141: \nL142: Manage your auto-play settings 【11†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBrowse chapters and episodes (https://help.audible.com/s/article/browse-chapters-and-episodes)\nciteturn764view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/browse-chapters-and-episodes\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 137\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Account & billing Alexa Android Ask A Question+5\nL13: ## Browse chapters and episodes\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 3, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Browse chapters and episodes\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: browse-chapters-and-episodes\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: No matter how you're listening, you can navigate between audiobook chapters or podcast episodes.\nL29: \nL30: In this article:\nL31:   * 【1†How can I browse chapters or podcast episodes in the player?】\nL32:   * 【2†How can I browse audiobook chapters or podcast episodes on my Fire TV?】\nL33:   * 【3†How can I browse audiobook chapters or podcast episodes on my Fire Tablet?】\nL34:   * 【4†Why don't the chapter numbers match my audiobook?】\nL35: ## How can I browse chapters or podcast episodes in the player?\nL36: \nL37: You can browse chapters or podcast episodes right from your player screen in the app or on your Cloud Player, or you can use Alexa voice commands to control Audible with any Alexa device.\nL38: \nL39: In the app player\nL40: \nL41:   1. In the player, select the Chapters menu icon.\nL42:   2. Select the chapter or episode you want to hear.\nL43: \nL44: On Cloud Player\nL45: \nL46:   1. In the player, select the Chapters icon.\nL47:   2. Select the chapter you want to hear.\nL48: ## How can I browse audiobook chapters or podcast episodes on my Fire TV?\nL49: \nL50: You can browse audiobook chapters or podcast episodes with the buttons on your paired Fire TV remote.\nL51: \nL52: Browse with your remote\nL53: \nL54:   1. Next to the title you want to hear, select Listen Now.\nL55:   2. When the player is open, select the Menu button on your remote.\nL56:   3. Select Chapters.\nL57:   4. Use the up and down buttons on the directional pad of your paired remote to navigate to a specific chapter.\nL58: \nL59: Browse with Alexa voice commands\nL60:   1. Press the microphone button on your remote.\nL61:   2. Try one of the following voice commands:\nL62:      * \"Alexa, next [chapter or episode].\"\nL63:      * \"Alexa, previous [chapter or episode].\"\nL64:      * \"Alexa, go to [chapter or episode] number [7].\"\nL65:      * \"Alexa, go to last [chapter or episode].\"\nL66: ## How can I browse audiobook chapters or podcast episodes on my Fire Tablet?\nL67: \nL68: You can browse chapters or podcast episodes right from your player screen in the app.\nL69: \nL70: In the app player\nL71: \nL72:   1. In the player, select the Chapters menu icon.\nL73:   2. Select the chapter or episode you want to hear.\nL74: ## Why don't the chapter numbers match my audiobook?\nL75: \nL76: Chapters in audiobooks may have numbers or names depending on how the audiobook was produced. In some cases, the chapter numbers in the Audible player may not perfectly align with the chapters in the physical or eBook version. Here's why:\nL77:   * Multi-part audiobooks: If the book is more than 8–10 hours or has more than 100 chapters, the audiobook will be split into several parts for a faster and easier download process.\nL78:   * Long chapters split into segments: Audiobooks with chapters that are longer than 2 hours will be broken down into smaller chapters to enhance the listening experience.\nL79:   * No chapter breakdown: Audiobooks with no chapter breakdown will be broken down into 30-minute segments to create easier navigation.\nL80:   * Short chapters grouped together: Audiobooks with very short chapters may be grouped together.\nL81: Note: If the chapter numbering in your audiobook seems incorrect and none of the above explanations apply, please contact the 【5†Audible Customer Service team†www.audible.com】 for assistance.\nL82: \nL83: Did this answer your question?\nL84: \nL85: 【6†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL86: \nL87: \nL88: \nL89: 【7†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL90: \nL91:  Back to top\nL92: \nL93: 【8†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL94: \nL95: 【9†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL96: ## Need more assistance?\nL97: \nL98: 【10†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL99: \nL100: \nL101: \nL102: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL103: \nL104: \nL105: \nL106: Worst\nL107: \nL108: 1\nL109: \nL110: 2\nL111: \nL112: 3\nL113: \nL114: 4\nL115: \nL116: 5\nL117: \nL118: 6\nL119: \nL120: 7\nL121: \nL122: Best\nL123: \nL124: \nL125: \nL126: Region\nL127: \nL128: United States\nL129: \nL130: Language\nL131: \nL132: English\nL133: \nL134: Loading\nL135: \nL136: Browse chapters and episodes 【11†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nView listening log (https://help.audible.com/s/article/view-listening-log?language=en_US)\nciteturn764view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/view-listening-log?language=en_US\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 142\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Android iOS Listening Player Player tools\nL13: ## View listening log\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 3, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: View listening log\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: view-listening-log\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: The Audible Listen Log is a feature that tracks your listening stats and activity. It shows you everything from when you first started a title to when you finished listening to it, including dates and times.\nL29: \nL30: In this article:\nL31:   * 【1†What is the Listen Log?】\nL32:   * 【2†What is the purpose of the Listen Log?】\nL33:   * 【3†How do I find my Listen Log?】\nL34:   * 【4†How do I view my Listening History?】\nL35:   * 【5†How do I remove a title from my Listening History?】\nL36: ## What is the Listen Log?\nL37: \nL38: Your Listen Log is a day-to-day record of your listening activity for a particular title. You can see the date and time you started listening, when you paused, and how long your listening session lasted.\nL39: \nL40: Notes:\nL41: \nL42:   * The Listen Log displays both dates and times for each session.\nL43:   * Listen Log data cannot be downloaded or exported.\nL44: ## What is the purpose of the Listen Log?\nL45: \nL46: The Listen Log can help you find your place if you get lost. It's a very useful tool if, for example:\nL47: \nL48:   * you fell asleep while listening and the book advanced without you;\nL49:   * you went back to an earlier chapter to re-listen to something, but didn't note where you had left off;\nL50:   * you accidentally moved the scrubber bar in the player and the book is now in a different section altogether.\nL51: Using the Listen Log, you can get back to the starting point of your last intentional listening section.\nL52: ## How do I find my Listen Log?\nL53: \nL54: The Listen Log is available only on the Audible app and can be accessed through these steps:\nL55: \nL56:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL57:   2. Open the player for a title you're currently enjoying or already finished.\nL58:   3. Select the Listen Log button below the cover of the book.\nL59: \nL60: From here, you can choose to replay a section or clear your entire history.\nL61: ## How do I view my Listening History?\nL62: \nL63: Your Listening History shows all the titles you've listened to over time.\nL64: \nL65: In the app\nL66: \nL67:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL68:   2. Go to your Profile.\nL69:   3. Swipe down to Activity & Stats.\nL70:   4. Select Listening History.\nL71: \nL72: On desktop\nL73: \nL74:   1. Go to the Audible site.\nL75:   2. Select your name on the top navigation.\nL76:   3. Select Listen History.\nL77: ## How do I remove a title from my Listening History?\nL78: \nL79: On desktop\nL80: \nL81:   1. Go to the Audible site.\nL82:   2. Select your name on the top navigation.\nL83:   3. Select Listen History.\nL84:   4. Select Remove next to the title you want to remove.\nL85: \nL86: Note: Listening History data cannot be downloaded or exported.\nL87: \nL88: Did this answer your question?\nL89: \nL90: 【6†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL91: \nL92: \nL93: \nL94: 【7†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL95: \nL96:  Back to top\nL97: \nL98: 【8†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL99: \nL100: 【9†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL101: ## Need more assistance?\nL102: \nL103: 【10†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL104: \nL105: \nL106: \nL107: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL108: \nL109: \nL110: \nL111: Worst\nL112: \nL113: 1\nL114: \nL115: 2\nL116: \nL117: 3\nL118: \nL119: 4\nL120: \nL121: 5\nL122: \nL123: 6\nL124: \nL125: 7\nL126: \nL127: Best\nL128: \nL129: \nL130: \nL131: Region\nL132: \nL133: United States\nL134: \nL135: Language\nL136: \nL137: English\nL138: \nL139: Loading\nL140: \nL141: View listening log 【11†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n"
